  "$delta_boundary_variance": "MEASURED 2026-10-16: the delta copies are NOT byte-identical in length. seq 0x73's payload is 7153 and 0x98/0x9a/0x9c/0x9e are 7154, because the position-carrying fragment (key=16, type_index=11) has a 48-byte payload in the first and 49 in the others - so the boundaries below describe 0x98/0x9a/0x9c/0x9e and slice 0x73 ONE BYTE LATE, which drops a fragment's leading key byte. A parse-then-encode round-trip cannot detect that (it is the identity for any bytes); the discriminator is the (key, type) pair per fragment, because the key->type binding is 1:1 and measured: a mis-sliced copy reports key=3857/type=2 where the client reported key=22/type=3857. This is why rep.py::compose_delta_position_bundle compares both tuples and refuses a body its boundaries do not describe. The live probe also reported the 48-byte form ([2, 60, 3955, 4295, 4301, 4498, 5335, 5385, 7124]) on 60/60 copies, so BOTH layouts occur live."
